## Common Patterns

### 1. Multiple Use Cases Pattern
```dart
group('init', () {
  group('when requests are successful', () {
    final popularMovies = [
      getFakeMovie(id: 1, title: 'Popular 1'),
    ];
    final upcomingMovies = [
      getFakeMovie(id: 2, title: 'Upcoming 1'),
    ];
    
    final mockGetPopularMovies = MockGetPopularMovies.dummy(movies: popularMovies);
    final mockGetUpcomingMovies = MockGetUpcomingMovies.dummy(movies: upcomingMovies);
    final homeBloc = getHomeBloc(
      getPopularMovies: mockGetPopularMovies,
      getUpcomingMovies: mockGetUpcomingMovies,
    );

    blocTest<HomeBloc, HomeState>(
      'emits correct state when both use cases return success',
      build: () => homeBloc,
      act: (bloc) => bloc.init(),
      expect: () => [
        isA<HomeState>()
            .having((state) => state.isLoading, 'isLoading', isTrue),
        isA<HomeState>()
            .having((state) => state.populaMovies.length, 'populaMovies loaded', 1)
            .having((state) => state.upcomingMovies.length, 'upcomingMovies loaded', 1)
            .having((state) => state.isLoading, 'isLoading', isFalse),
      ],
    );
  });
});
```

### 2. Error Priority Pattern
```dart
group('when both use cases fail', () {
  final mockGetPopularMovies = MockGetPopularMovies();
  final mockGetUpcomingMovies = MockGetUpcomingMovies();
  final popularMoviesError = ServerError(statusCode: 500);
  final upcomingMoviesError = ConnectionError();

  when(() => mockGetPopularMovies.call()).thenAnswer(
    (_) async => Failure(popularMoviesError),
  );
  when(() => mockGetUpcomingMovies.call()).thenAnswer(
    (_) async => Failure(upcomingMoviesError),
  );

  final homeBloc = getHomeBloc(
    getPopularMovies: mockGetPopularMovies,
    getUpcomingMovies: mockGetUpcomingMovies,
  );

  blocTest<HomeBloc, HomeState>(
    'emits error state when both use cases fail',
    build: () => homeBloc,
    act: (bloc) => bloc.init(),
    expect: () => [
      // Loading state
      isA<HomeState>().having((state) => state.isLoading, 'isLoading', isTrue),
      // Error state (should use first error as it's checked first)
      isA<HomeState>()
          .having((state) => state.error, 'error', isA<ServerError>()),
    ],
  );
});
```

## Enforcement Guidelines

### 1. Code Review Checklist
- [ ] Test follows group structure pattern
- [ ] Creates test data first, then mocks, then BLoCs
- [ ] Uses `final` for all declarations (no `late` keyword)
- [ ] Uses helper functions for BLoC creation
- [ ] Uses dummy mock methods for success scenarios
- [ ] Uses `when().thenAnswer()` for error scenarios
- [ ] Registers fallback values for complex types
- [ ] Tests both success and error scenarios
- [ ] Uses fake data generators
- [ ] Follows naming conventions
- [ ] Includes proper state assertions

### 2. Linting Rules
- Enable Flutter test analyzer rules
- Check for unused imports
- Validate test structure
- Ensure proper mock usage

### 3. Test Execution
```bash
# Run specific BLoC tests
flutter test test/presentation/home/home_bloc_test.dart

# Run all BLoC tests
flutter test test/presentation/

# Run with coverage
flutter test --coverage
```

---

These guidelines ensure consistent, maintainable, and comprehensive BLoC testing throughout the MovieAlike project. Follow these patterns for all new BLoC tests and refactor existing tests to match these standards.
